	(text "NIBBLE CARD COUPON: every cell of the machine in copper, measured before any card is trusted"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8c4ca3d7-479d-48aa-b603-6e352a5b298d")
	)
	(text "57 transistors, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).  Power: 5 V on the 2-pin header from the bench supply (limit 300 mA),\nor the bus header (the hub; no other bus line is used).\nDrive IN, N1, N2, N3, RST from the 6-pin header (each has a 1Meg pull-down, so open = 0; RST open lets the flip-flop run).\nMeasure at the test loops: RING period (gate delay = period / 10; RING0 is the ring node itself, for when the buffer's threshold is above the ring's swing),\nFO1 vs FO10 rise time (fan-out 1 vs 10),\nNAND / NOR low with all three inputs high, BUS low with the hub's 10k, X (the Schmitt trip points) and OSC (the clock card's\noscillator, 100k + 47n), Q (the toggle flip-flop, OSC / 2; RST high holds it at 0), DRV (the D053 line driver, clip 3.3 nF on it),\nVTO (about 0.1 V above one transistor's threshold), ROM (a program row through its diode into 220k), the supply current.\nThe bands to expect at each loop: sim/results/coupon_expected.md; how to read them: docs/bring-up.md section 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "468253d8-60ec-4837-b1dd-b2410fd5cc8b")
	)
